# Working on LLM OS

You are the coding agent for LLM OS, working inside VS Code on the owner's Mac. The project is open source and published on GitHub.

Before starting any task, read these in order:
1. Support files/docs/HANDOFF-TO-NEXT-AI.md (mandate, owner's corrections, architecture, current state, open items in section 7)
2. Support files/docs/PROJECT-CONTEXT.md
3. Support files/docs/tasks/queue.md (the task queue; finished items go to queue-done.md)

Rules:
- Work only inside this project folder. Never touch other folders on the Mac.
- The OS code is Python with no third-party libraries, under Support files/src/rootfs/. Keep it that way.
- Run host tests only with `bash "Support files/tools/run-host-tests.sh"`. Redirect output to a file and read the summary; never trust a piped tail. A change is done only when the suite passes.
- Gate every OTA publish on the suite: `run-host-tests.sh > log && tools/ota.py publish ...`.
- selfdev.py refuses to run on a live install on purpose. Never remove that guard.
- The x86 laptop (tools/devssh.py, tools/devlink.py) is the only real install. Never restart its network services remotely. Run one VM at a time.
- Never read, print, commit or send anything in Support files/ota-keys/. Never commit images, ISOs, models or build output; .gitignore already excludes them.
- Commit each finished change with a clear message describing what changed and why. The owner pushes to GitHub from VS Code's Source Control panel.
- If something is unclear, read the docs and code first. Do not guess file names or variables; open the file.
